We isolate the functions responsible for the violations and input them into an online tool, Compiler Explorer~\cite{CompilerExplorer}, which includes the \textit{Opt Pipeline} and \textit{GCC Tree/RTL} viewer tools.
This allows us to finely explore the impact of each optimization pass, as well as their interactions with each other, and determine precisely how they break constant-time guarantees for LLVM and GCC respectively.

