The Q-Q plots (Figures 8 and 9) provide a visualization of tail heaviness. Model 1, with only LHS, demonstrates some heavy tails, though most values align with the 45-degree line, indicating a challenge in capturing full model complexity. In contrast, Model 2 (LHS + GP) shows heavier tails, especially for \( t_{h, \text{eff}} \), underscoring the increased complexity captured by incorporating GP.

