\subsection{Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:low-depth-LRFC-designs}: The blocked LRFC circuit has small measurable error}  \label{sec: pf blocked LRFC}


Finally, we can address the blocked LRFC circuit.
%
Similar to our proof of nearly optimal state designs, we will project onto a tensor product of \emph{local} distinct subspaces $\PD^a$ on each patch $a$ of $\xi$ qubits.
%
%Here, a patch $a$ is a set of $\xi$ qubits that is the overlap of any patch of $2\xi$ qubits in the odd circuit layers and any patch of $2\xi$ qubits in the even circuit layers.
%
Motivated by our analysis of the LRFC ensemble,
we will divide these patches into two alternating subsets: even patches, which are shuffled by $S_e$ in the second circuit layer, and odd patches, which are shuffled by $S_o$ in the fifth layer.
%
We let 
\begin{equation}
    \PD^{\text{loc}(o)} = \bigotimes_{a \in \text{odd}} \PD^a \,\,\,\,\,\, \text{ and } \,\,\,\,\,\,
    \PD^{\text{loc}(e)} = \bigotimes_{a \in \text{even}} \PD^a
\end{equation}
denote the local distinct subspace projectors on the odd and even patches, respectively.
These will play an analogous role to $\PD^L$ and $\PD^R$ in our LRFC proof.
%
The subspaces have dimensions $\mathfrak{D}_{e} =\mathfrak{D}_{o} = 2^{(n/2)k} \cdot (\mathfrak{D}_a)^{m/2} \geq 2^{nk} (1-k^2/2^{\xi})^{m/2} \geq 2^{nk}(1 - \tilde \delta)$ where $\tilde \delta \equiv (m/2) k^2/2^\xi$, where $\mathfrak{D}_a = (2^\xi)!/(2^\xi-k+1)!$ is the dimension of each patch.



% %
% We write this projector as $\PD^{\text{loc}} = \bigotimes_{a=1}^{m} \PD^a$, where $\PD^a$ is the distinct subspace projector on each patch $a$ and $m \equiv n/\xi$.

% %
% The local distinct subspace has dimension $\mathfrak{D}_{\text{loc}} = (\mathfrak{D}_a)^{m} \geq 2^{nk} (1-k^2/2^{\xi})^m \geq 2^{nk}(1 - \delta'')$ for $\delta'' \equiv m k^2/2^\xi$, where $\mathfrak{D}_a = (2^\xi)!/(2^\xi-k+1)!$ is the dimension on each patch.


With this setup in hand, our proof proceeds nearly identically to  PFC and LRFC.
