\section{Numerical Experiments \label{sec:experiments}}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

We now present numerical experiments supporting our theoretical results. First, we benchmark the trainability of LCE transformed PQCs using the Taylor surrogate to confirm that proper Clifford design yields constant-scaling gradients (cf. Theorems~\ref{thm:general-escaping-barren-plateau} and~\ref{thm:quantum-advantage}). We then apply these insights to VQE optimization, leveraging improved gradients on near-Clifford patches.

\subsection{Initial Gradient Scalability}
