We evaluate the scaling of the gradient norm $\|(\nabla_\theta\,C)(0)\|$ for increasing qubit numbers $N$ focusing on the \texttt{mHEA}~\cite{leone2024HEA} model—a minimalistic Hardware-Efficient Ansatz based on Qiskit’s \texttt{EfficientSU2}~\cite{efficientsu2}, comprising $Y$/$Z$-rotations and circular entanglement. 
Appendix~\ref{sec:ansatz} shows additional PQC models with their respective LCE modifications. Note that Theorem~\ref{thm:general-escaping-barren-plateau} applies in general even to deep PQCs.

\begin{figure}[h]
    \centering
