\section{A closer look at the OLG Model}
\label{sec:OLG}
The Object Logic Graph specifies a set of node and relationship types together with their semantics (Table \ref{tab:graph_model}). Nodes and edges are allowed to  have additional attributes to characterize their specific properties. Consider a municipal code from the city of Carlsbad -- ``a food truck vendor may sell or offer to sell merchandise, food or beverages from a food truck only at the request of a bona fide purchaser and may not park or stand for longer than 60 minutes on any public street, alley, highway, parking lot, sidewalk or right-of-way''. The nodes in an OLG representation of the code can be represented as shown in Table  \ref{tab:nodes} while the edges are shown in Figure \ref{fig:graph_visualization}.
