\subsection{2D}

In higher dimensions, we are interested in the maximum $\norm{\boldsymbol{\nu}}$ for which our method remains stable. To simplify the problem, we note that the most challenging case for a given $\norm{\boldsymbol{\nu}}$ occurs when $\nu_1 = \nu_2$. Therefore, we perform our von Neumann analysis with $\nu_1 = \nu_2$ and $100^2$ evenly sampled wave Numbers. Figure \ref{fig:amplification-2D} shows the amplification factor. The scheme is stable for CFL values of around $0.7 \approx 1 / \sqrt{2}$. 

