The performance gain is also significant in categories with high intra-class variance, such as \textit{Red winged Blackbird} and \textit{Groove billed Ani}, where traditional prompt tuning suffers due to under-generalized static prompts. Our model mitigates this by generating input-specific prompts that align better with visual semantics.

This result demonstrates that our method is not only strong in average performance but also offers consistent advantages in detailed category-level classification, which is crucial for applications such as biodiversity monitoring or species identification.




